      "Do not expand to sound smarter. Padding academic or professional writing with elaborate phrasing often backfires — experienced readers see through it, and it can make your actual ideas harder to find.",
      "Do not expand dialogue or personal voice passages. The expander's formal patterns will flatten the natural rhythm of conversational writing. If a passage works because it sounds like you, expanding it will make it sound less like you.",
      "And do not expand the same way twice. If every paragraph in your document has the same expanded rhythm, the whole piece starts to feel artificial. Vary your approach.",
      "## Tips for the Best Results",
      "Get more out of the tool with these practices.",
      "Start with clear input. The expander works best on grammatically clean sentences with a clear subject and verb. If your input is fragmented or confusing, the output will be longer but equally confusing. Fix the input first.",
      "Expand in small chunks. Feed the tool one paragraph at a time rather than a whole document. This gives you control over each section and makes editing manageable.",
      "Choose the right expansion level. A light expansion adds a little detail; a heavy expansion transforms the text substantially. Match the level to your need — light for polishing, heavy for first drafts.",
      "Edit ruthlessly afterward. Read the expanded output and cut everything that does not earn its place. Ask of each added phrase: does this add meaning, or just words? Keep the meaning, cut the words.",
      "Mix expanded and original sentences. A paragraph where every sentence has been expanded sounds monotonous. Expand the sentences that need it; leave the strong ones alone. Contrast creates rhythm.",
      "Add your own specifics. The expander adds generic elaboration — it cannot add your examples, your data, or your experience. After expanding, insert one concrete detail of your own. That single addition often does more for the paragraph than all the expansion combined.",
      "## A Worked Example",
      "Input: \"Regular exercise improves health.\"",
      "Light expansion might produce: \"Regular exercise genuinely improves overall health, supporting both physical fitness and mental well-being in meaningful ways.\"",
      "That is better — but notice it is still generic. Now add your own edit: \"Regular exercise genuinely improves health — even a daily 20-minute walk lowered my resting heart rate within two months.\"",
      "The final version is longer than the input, but more importantly it is specific, personal, and credible. That is the pattern to aim for: expand, then humanize with your own detail.",
      "## Privacy Note",
      "Like all our tools, the Sentence Expander runs completely in your browser. Your text is processed locally and never sent to a server. Drafts, unpublished work, and personal writing stay on your device.",
      "## The Bottom Line",
